  "transcript_source": "captions",
  "transcript": [
    {
      "s": 9.23,
      "e": 12.48,
      "text": "(tape fast forwarding)"
    },
    {
      "s": 21.61,
      "e": 23.76,
      "text": "- [Bill] This is a two and a half minute tape"
    },
    {
      "s": 23.76,
      "e": 28.49,
      "text": "of the damage caused by a tornado that hit Jackson, Alabama"
    },
    {
      "s": 28.49,
      "e": 32.92,
      "text": "on the 24th of March, 1984."
    },
    {
      "s": 34.29,
      "e": 35.53,
      "text": "My name is Bill Ralston"
    },
    {
      "s": 35.53,
      "e": 39.55,
      "text": "with the Emergency Management Division here in Mobile."
    },
    {
      "s": 41.5,
      "e": 46.5,
      "text": "This tornado hit about 8:00 PM, 2000 hours,"
    },
    {
      "s": 46.6,
      "e": 48.2,
      "text": "Saturday the 24th."
    },
    {
      "s": 50.01,
      "e": 53.08,
      "text": "It struck the Jackson Academy, a private school,"
    },
    {
      "s": 53.96,
      "e": 55.66,
      "text": "which received extensive damage."
    },
    {
      "s": 56.73,
      "e": 60.23,
      "text": "You can see the automobiles here, about 25 automobiles"
    },
    {
      "s": 60.23,
      "e": 63.0,
      "text": "that were heavily damaged,"
    },
    {
      "s": 63.0,
      "e": 68.0,
      "text": "and we sent a recon team up there about 10:00 PM that night."
    },
    {
      "s": 69.7,
      "e": 74.45,
      "text": "And we did that under the authority of AR 560."
    },
    {
      "s": 76.35,
      "e": 79.7,
      "text": "You can see the local people cleaning up the damage."
    },
    {
      "s": 80.57,
      "e": 85.14,
      "text": "It was about $500,000 in damage to the private school"
    },
    {
      "s": 88.85,
      "e": 90.94,
      "text": "and to an apartment complex."
    },
    {
      "s": 90.94,
      "e": 95.26,
      "text": "This is the Channel Five TV network taking pictures"
    },
    {
      "s": 95.26,
      "e": 96.78,
      "text": "of the area on Sunday."
    },
    {
      "s": 96.78,
      "e": 99.2,
      "text": "Now these video pictures were taken"
    },
    {
      "s": 99.2,
      "e": 101.19,
      "text": "on Sunday, the 25th of March."
    },
    {
      "s": 102.51,
      "e": 107.51,
      "text": "It was three houses destroyed and two house trailers,"
    },
    {
      "s": 109.41,
      "e": 114.41,
      "text": "small businesses and the one apartment complex"
    },
    {
      "s": 114.44,
      "e": 115.89,
      "text": "with four units."
    },
    {
      "s": 115.89,
      "e": 119.53,
      "text": "Electrical power was out and telephone lines were damaged."
    },
    {
      "s": 119.53,
      "e": 122.83,
      "text": "No death or injuries occurred."
    },
    {
      "s": 122.83,
      "e": 126.26,
      "text": "And it was a small tornado, but we were real lucky."
    },
    {
      "s": 126.26,
      "e": 129.03,
      "text": "It was a graduation class that night,"
    },
    {
      "s": 129.03,
      "e": 133.63,
      "text": "which the tornado missed by a couple of hundred yards."
    },
    {
      "s": 134.84,
      "e": 136.89,
      "text": "You can see some of the debris scattered."
    },
    {
      "s": 138.7,
      "e": 141.86,
      "text": "(page turning)"
    },
    {
      "s": 141.86,
      "e": 143.69,
      "text": "The state and local governments,"
    },
    {
      "s": 144.95,
      "e": 147.36,
      "text": "they handled the situation real good."
    },
    {
      "s": 147.36,
      "e": 150.44,
      "text": "So the court didn't receive any requests"
    },
    {
      "s": 150.44,
      "e": 154.08,
      "text": "for assistance under this emergency."
    },
    {
      "s": 156.9,
      "e": 160.12,
      "text": "(page turning)"
    },
    {
      "s": 160.12,
      "e": 162.92,
      "text": "It's not anticipated that a disaster declaration"
    },
    {
      "s": 162.92,
      "e": 167.86,
      "text": "would be issued since it was fairly small disaster."
    }
  ],
